  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Fair weather persists thru today under \nweak mid and upper level flow across the great Basin. Skies will \nbe mostly sunny though high level clouds begin to move in from the\nsouthwest. \n\nAn upper level low off the coast of SoCal will continue to \nadvance east and begin to move inland tonight. The low will enter\nsouthern Nevada Monday advecting sufficient moisture into the\nregion to produce rain showers and thunderstorms. Better \nagreement for moisture availability is still noted within the \nmost recent numerical model solutions. PWATs of 0.5-0.7 inches \nwill push to the northeast and into the forecast are under the \nsouth- southwesterly flow circulating around the low. Showers and \nthunderstorms move into central Nevada Monday with activity moving\nin from the southwest. Activity spreads into eastern Nevada and \nElko County Monday night and Tuesday. The best opportunity for \naccumulating rainfall will be across central Nevada and \nspecifically White Pine County. ECMWF guidance has rainfall \naccumulations of 0.1-0.2 inches across White Pine County.\n\nThe system will exit the area on Wednesday riding the flow of its\nparent trof centered off the western Canadian coast. A transition\nto southwesterly flow will be present over the western U.S. the \nremainder of the week. This will produce fair weather across the \nGreat Basin beginning Wednesday and thru the rest of the work \nweek, leading to a gradual warming trend thru Friday. Afternoon \nhigh temperatures will climb back into the low to mid 80s. \nMeanwhile a robust upper level trof will deepen and progress east \ninto the western U.S. from the Gulf of Alaska the latter portion \nof the week. Weather looks to remain dry at this time though \nbreezes will become more prevalent by Friday and Saturday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence remains in a\nquiet forecast through today. Moderate confidence exists in \nshower and thunderstorm activity on Monday and Tuesday. Again \nopted for a blend of various model guidance to produce a more \naccurate PoP and weather forecast thru the period.",
